# closed-method-set-with-session-result-reuse

The set of permitted validation and analytical methods is closed: use only the explicitly enumerated methods (e.g., WHOIS, DNS, EXIF, timestamps). Do not propose, add, or substitute alternatives even when they appear equivalent. Additionally, before re-running a validation step, check whether a prior validated result for the same artifact exists in the session; if so, reference that result rather than repeating the analysis.

## Procedures
- Before executing a validation step, check session history for a prior validated result on the same artifact (e.g., same SSL host, same domain).
- If a prior result exists and has not been flagged with an integrity or consistency issue, reference its validated digest/data rather than re-running the analysis.
- Use only the prescribed validation methods — never propose or execute an alternative method not in the enumerated set.
- When the prescribed method set is insufficient to answer a question, surface that gap explicitly rather than substituting an unlisted method.

## Conventions
- Reference previously validated SSL chain digests by their internal digest identifier before initiating fresh chain analysis.
- Document the session-prior result citation inline in the output when reusing a cached result.

